[38;5;252m[1m## The real bug found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The translation was logically correct but [1mnot bit-identical for NaN inputs[22m. On x86-64, [38;5;10maddss[0m/[38;5;10mmulss[0m with two NaN operands returns the payload in the [3mdestination[23m register, and gcc [38;5;10m-O0[0m picks different destination registers than LLVM. That surfaced as NaN sign-bit mismatches in [38;5;10mc2Dot[0m, [38;5;10mc2Det2[0m, [38;5;10mc2Add[0m, [38;5;10mc2Mulrv[0m, [38;5;10mc2MulrvT[0m, [38;5;10mc2Witness[0m, [38;5;10mc2L[0m, [38;5;10mc22[0m, [38;5;10mc23[0m, [38;5;10mc2CircletoCircle[0m and [38;5;10mc2CircletoCapsule[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
